    {
      "id": "bt_qtxt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58,
      "y": 558,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "roughness": 0,
      "text": "\"the easiest way to spot a primary LVN is just look all the way to the right and see which ones are closest\nthink of it an inverse and so the deepest one's primary\"   — Volume Profile 101, lines 81-86",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "createdAt": "2026-08-30T20:39:50.475Z",
